            "subject": "LU-930 doc: Fix typos in OSD API documentation"
          }
        ],
        "author": {
          "name": "Oleg Drokin",
          "email": "green@whamcloud.com",
          "date": "2026-09-09 04:00:18.000000000",
          "tz": -240
        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Oleg Drokin",
          "email": "green@whamcloud.com",
          "date": "2026-09-10 03:31:36.000000000",
          "tz": -240
        },
        "subject": "LU-20725 osd-ldiskfs: run commit callbacks newest first",
        "message": "LU-20725 osd-ldiskfs: run commit callbacks newest first\n\nAn MDS soft lockup panics the jbd2 commit thread in\nptlrpc_commit_replies() under a metadata create load.\n\nosd_trans_txn_cb() runs the commit's callbacks in registration order,\nso tgt_cb_last_committed() raises exp_last_committed one transno at a\ntime and ptlrpc_commit_replies() rescans the whole export uncommitted\nreply list each time.  With sync lock cancel that list held 8069\nreplies in the crash dump, and 6930 callbacks were still queued.\next4-jcb-optimization.patch reversed the order for older ldiskfs.\n\nQueue the extra handles at the head so the callbacks run newest\nregistration first, which normally commits the highest transno first\nand lets the rest take the tgt_cb_last_committed() fast path.\n100k creates on 2 MDTs: 2.2e9 list steps scanned before, 1.0e5 after.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial serverdistro=el10.2 testlist=performance-sanity\nFixes: 5744762a5a38 (\"LU-19142 osd-ldiskfs: journal commit callback\")\nSigned-off-by: Oleg Drokin <green@whamcloud.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:Opus-5 llm_code_and_review_tools\nChange-Id: Idf1578be0fa2434ebae511118ec2217acab3ddfb\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
